.TH REMAP_FILE_PAGES 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
remap_file_pages \- invokes deprecated linux remap_file_pages on a shared file mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B int remap_file_pages(void* address, size_t size, int protection, size_t page_offset, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes deprecated Linux remap_file_pages on a shared file mapping. Modern kernels emulate it; it can change an existing mapping.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR remap_file_pages (2)
